NV_PK(7,{"rice cake":"","a soft cake made from rice flour or rice batter":"","wa gui is a steamed rice cake in a bowl":"","batter":"","a thick liquid of flour or ground rice and water":"","pour the rice batter into small bowls":"","bamboo spatula":"","a small flat piece of bamboo used like a knife or spoon":"","cut the wa gui with a bamboo spatula":"","brunch":"","fish floss":"","dried fish pulled into soft fluffy threads":"","sprinkle fish floss on the sticky rice":"","rice cakes like red turtle cakes are also temple offerings each with a lucky meaning":"","use the bamboo stick to cut it into pieces":"","it's smooth and full of rice flavour":"","a meal eaten late in the morning between breakfast and lunch":"","let's have a tainan brunch":"","stir fried eel noodles are a high flame dish you mostly find in tainan the cook throws strips of eel onion and cabbage into a wok flames shoot up and in seconds it is done with the eel still crunchy":"","yi noodles are egg noodles that have been fried first so they are curly springy and soak up the sauce you can order them dry fried or in a thick glossy sauce the sauce is tainan style sweet and sour with sugar and black vinegar":"","because every plate has to be cooked fast over a huge flame one at a time there is often a queue watching the cook toss the wok in a burst of fire is part of the show":""});